      "text": "To solve the problem \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\), we can use the difference of squares formula, which states that \\(a^2 - b^2 = (a - b)(a + b)\\). Here, \\(a = 235\\) and \\(b = 221\\).\n\nFirst, we apply the difference of squares formula:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = (235 - 221)(235 + 221)\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(235 - 221\\):\n\\[\n235 - 221 = 14\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(235 + 221\\):\n\\[\n235 + 221 = 456\n\\]\n\nNow, substitute these values back into the expression:\n\\[\n235^2 - 221^2 = 14 \\times 456\n\\]\n\nNext, we need to compute \\(14 \\times 456\\):\n\\[\n14 \\times 456 = 14 \\times (450 + 6) = 14 \\times 450 + 14 \\times 6\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(14 \\times 450\\):\n\\[\n14 \\times 450 = 6300\n\\]\n\nCalculate \\(14 \\times 6\\):\n\\[\n14 \\times 6 = 84\n\\]\n\nAdd these two results together:\n\\[\n6300 + 84 = 6384\n\\]\n\nNow, we need to divide this result by 14:\n\\[\n\\frac{6384}{14} = 456\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(\\frac{235^2 - 221^2}{14}\\) is \\(\\boxed{456}\\).",
